id=a52sxq_soundtrigger_load_no_reboot
name=Sound trigger: a refused model load no longer restarts the audio HAL, and a busy refusal is retried
author=kusti420
description=Tester log 2026-10-20 (logsrecentes.txt): "Hey Google" (vendor UUID 7038ddc8-30f2-11e6-b0ac-40a8f03d3f15) was loaded while audio played; the A52s HIDL sound trigger HAL took the non-LPI path ('lpi NOT supported due to concurrency') and ape_reg_sm failed to open the ADSP listen session (/dev/snd/pcmC0D10c 'Out of memory', status -19 = -ENODEV, 5 HAL retries). The audio side is the stock A14 one (sound_trigger_platform_info.xml, mixer paths, ACDB, sound_trigger.primary.lahaina.so, q6_dlkm/platform_dlkm all byte-identical to SM-A528B), and stock A14 services.jar maps every load status to HalException and reboots the HAL too, so stock had no deferral either. The 'no LSM table for 602/app_type 3' ACDB lines are not the cause: the HAL's boot probe of the same Google non-LPI usecase prints them and opens pcmC0D10c fine (test phone 2026-10-22), and Bixby (app_type 5) re-registers non-LPI during playback fine. The -ENOMEM comes from the kernel LSM client alloc (no free LSM session / APR port), a resource refusal. 9.3.63: HalException on load -> RecoverableException(INTERNAL_ERROR) instead of SoundTriggerHalEnforcer rebooting the HAL (= the whole audio HAL process: audio + BT audio drop, audioserver restart). Now K4StRetry (src/) reports -ENODEV/-EBUSY/-ENOMEM/-EAGAIN as RESOURCE_CONTENTION, the AOSP status for this: SoundTriggerHelper keeps the model requested, tells the client onRecognitionPaused() and loads it again on onResourcesAvailable(). A HIDL 2.x HAL never sends that callback (AIDL HALs do), so K4StRetry sends it on the HAL stack's global callback when the HAL's concurrency ends: all playback stopped (+5 s for audio HAL output standby) or screen off (+2 s, LPI path). One retry per event, no timers. Other load statuses stay INTERNAL_ERROR. A HAL status refusal of a load never reboots: the enforcer records a model only after a successful load, so a refusal leaves nothing to resync. A load that fails otherwise (not a HalException) or hangs past the 3 s watchdog deadline is handled like any other HAL error. Every other HAL error is handled by soundtrigger_no_hal_reboot through the same K4StRetry (outside calls: reboot after a 3 s grace with the mode re-read; during calls - audio mode, telephony call state of any SIM, or voice/ringtone playback or voice recording - after the call). onResourcesAvailable runs on its own thread (K4StRetryCb), never on the thread that decides reboots, because it takes the SoundTriggerModule monitor that a hung HAL call holds. The screen-off / audio-stopped retry holds a partial wakelock for delay + 1 s. K4StRetry forgets a HAL stack when it is detached (SoundTriggerHalEnforcer.detach, called from SoundTriggerModule.binderDied), so dead stacks are not kept or retried. Watchdog timeouts (hung HAL call) are deferred during calls too (soundtrigger_no_hal_reboot). Telephony calls: AOSP/stock DeviceStateHandler unloads sound models for the call and reloads them after it, by design.
